<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 3.02 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 3.02 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0675 to the dollar, up from 3.0695 on Tuesday and at 1.8345 to the mark, up from 1.8390, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.02 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Tuesday's 2.89 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
